  "id": "romanian_colindat_ceata",
  "name": "Colindat (Romanian men's-group Christmas carolling)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Christmas-time house-to-house carolling of Romanian villages, performed by a ceată, an organised group of young unmarried men who rehearse beforehand under a chosen leader and on Christmas Eve sing colinde at each house, wishing the household health and plenty and receiving gifts in return. Inscribed by UNESCO in 2013 for Romania and Moldova, it is especially strong in Transylvania, including Hunedoara, where the group often divides in two to sing alternate verses. Béla Bartók and Constantin Brăiloiu documented its texts and its distinctive asymmetric syllabic rhythms.",
  "recipe": "classic early-2010s colindat, carnival Processional, European branch. one note per syllable, two spatially opposed choirs. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
